 "old_string": "Thus palette/separator color can vary: re-identify separator lines, background and sparse marker from each instance, and count markers per panel. This is task-specific evidence; if a future same-ID variant differs, replay its demonstrations before applying the rule.",
 "new_string": "Thus palette/separator color can vary: re-identify separator lines, background and sparse marker from each instance, and count markers per panel. This is task-specific evidence; if a future same-ID variant differs, replay its demonstrations before applying the rule.\n\nAdditional accepted variant: an 8×19 grid had full separator rows 2 and 5 and separator columns 3, 7, 11, 15 (zero-based); the remaining 3×5 panels were each 2×3. Background was 7 and sparse marker was 3; separator color was 2. Counts by panel row were `[1,1,1,1,2]`, `[1,2,1,1,1]`, `[1,1,2,1,1]`. Applying `count >= 2 → 1`, otherwise 7 yielded `[[7,7,7,7,1],[7,1,7,7,7],[7,7,1,7,7]]`, which was accepted. This reinforces that panels are defined by separator stripes, not fixed square shapes, and each marker count is independent."
